## Security Considerations

### Secret-Based Authentication

Brand applications validate incoming events using the `X-A2B-Brand-Secret` header:

```typescript
// In agency-event-handler
const isRegistrationEvent = 
  params.type === 'com.adobe.a2b.registration.received' ||
  params.type === 'com.adobe.a2b.registration.enabled';

if (!isRegistrationEvent) {
  const headers = params.__ow_headers || {};
  const brandSecret = headers['x-a2b-brand-secret'];
  
  if (!brandSecret) {
    return errorResponse(401, 'Missing X-A2B-Brand-Secret header', logger);
  }
  
  // Validate secret against stored agency configuration
  const agency = await agencyManager.getAgency(agencyId);
  if (!agency.validateSecret(brandSecret)) {
    return errorResponse(401, 'Invalid brand secret', logger);
  }
}
```

**Exception**: Registration events (`registration.received`, `registration.enabled`) bypass secret validation because the brand doesn't have the secret yet during initial registration.

### Agency Identification

The agency ID is extracted from `app_runtime_info.consoleId`:

```typescript
const agencyId = eventData.app_runtime_info?.consoleId;
if (!agencyId) {
  return errorResponse(400, 'Missing agencyId in app_runtime_info', logger);
}
```

This ensures events are properly attributed to the correct agency instance.
